// ================== Verifiable Membership (signed change log) ==================
//
// Every membership mutation of a CHANNEL_PUBLIC / CHANNEL_PRIVATE channel is a
// ChannelChange signed by its author's ACI identity key and hash-chained to the
// previous MembershipState. The server stores, serialises (one revision at a
// time) and relays changes and still keeps plaintext membership for routing and
// SpiceDB, but clients decide who receives sender keys from the verified state
// only. The server re-verifies every change as defence in depth; no client
// relies on that.
//
// ---- Signatures (domain-separated XEdDSA, libsignal PrivateKey::calculate_signature) ----
//    signature    = XEdDSA(author identity key,
//                          "chatter-channel-change-v1\0" || actions)
//    invite_proof = XEdDSA(invite private key,
//                          "chatter-channel-invite-v1\0" || actions)
// `actions` is the exact byte string the author serialised. It is signed and
// parsed but NEVER re-serialised by anyone, so protobuf serializer determinism
// does not matter for signatures. ("\0" is one 0x00 byte.)
//
// ---- State hash ----
//    state_hash = SHA-256("chatter-channel-state-v1\0" || canonical_state)
// canonical_state is NOT the protobuf encoding of MembershipState. It is
// (all integers big-endian, "str"/"bin" = u32 length prefix then the bytes):
//    u8   format version            = 1
//    str  channel_id                (lowercase hyphenated UUID, UTF-8)
//    u64  revision
//    u8   policy.add_member         (ChannelRole number)
//    u8   policy.remove_member
//    u8   policy.set_role
//    u8   policy.manage_invites
//    u8   policy.set_disappearing
//    u8   policy.join               (AccessPolicy.JoinMode number)
//    u32  disappearing_seconds
//    u32  member count, then per member, sorted ascending by the bytes of user_id:
//           str  user_id            (lowercase hyphenated UUID)
//           u8   role               (ChannelRole number)
//           u8   status             (StateMember.Status number)
//           bin  identity_key       (33 bytes: 0x05 || Curve25519 public key)
//    u32  invite count, then per invite, sorted ascending by the bytes of invite_pub:
//           bin  invite_pub         (33 bytes: 0x05 || Curve25519 public key)
//           u8   role
//           u64  expires_at         (Unix nanoseconds; 0 = never)
//           u32  max_uses           (0 = unlimited)
//           u32  uses
//           u8   needs_approval     (0 or 1)
// Duplicate user_ids / invite_pubs, unknown enum numbers, non-canonical
// UUIDs, and anything but exactly one OWNER (who is ACTIVE) make a state
// invalid. The empty state before genesis has no hash: the
// genesis change (revision 1) carries an EMPTY prev_state_hash.
// Golden vectors: internal/services/channel/membership/testdata/membership_vectors.json

/// Who may do what. Every field must be set (no UNSPECIFIED) in a valid state.
/// Clients author these defaults: add_member ADMIN, remove_member MODERATOR,
/// set_role ADMIN, manage_invites ADMIN, set_disappearing ADMIN; join
